    perk or reward, or as a bundled component of a server or product you sell
    or distribute;

(d) modify, adapt, translate, port or create Derivative Works of the Software,
    except for (i) editing configuration files as intended, and (ii)
    Contributions made under Section 2.3 and Section 4.4;

(e) re-implement, in any language, engine or platform, the Software's source
    code, structure, sequence and organization, class, specialization, ability
    and path-tree systems, formulas, balance tables, configuration schema, or
    item and crafting data, to the extent they are protected by law. This
    clause does not restrict independent creation of a work that neither
    copies nor is derived from the protected expression of the Software, and
    does not restrict ideas, methods or functional elements that law leaves
    unprotected;

(f) decompile, disassemble, reverse engineer, deobfuscate or attempt to derive
    source code from compiled Software, except to the limited extent that
    applicable law expressly permits despite this restriction (for example,
    for interoperability);

(g) remove, alter, hide or falsify any copyright notice, source header, SPDX
    identifier, license file, attribution, watermark, fingerprint, identifier,
    license check or other technical protection measure in the Software, or
    circumvent or disable any of them;

(h) use the Software, its source code, documentation, configuration or data to
    train, fine-tune, evaluate or build any machine-learning model, dataset or
    index, or scrape or mine the repository by automated means for such
    purposes. This does not prohibit interactive use of an AI assistant by
    Authorized Personnel or Authorized Contributors to work on the Software
